crabbyavif: remove disable_cfi no_sanitize attributes for Rust 1.91+

Rust 1.91 removed the no_sanitize feature attribute that earlier compilers
accepted. The vendored crabbyavif crate gates a handful of functions behind
#[cfg_attr(feature = "disable_cfi", no_sanitize(cfi))] and the matching
#![cfg_attr(feature = "disable_cfi", feature(no_sanitize))] crate attribute,
which the build does not enable (disable_cfi is not in this recipe's feature
list), so rustc rejects the attribute outright regardless.

Remove the unreachable attribute and its matching feature declaration. No
functional change: the attribute was never active in this build.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Yocto toolchain workaround for a vendored
Chromium third-party crate; not a Chromium or crabbyavif upstream change]

